    <div style="background:#10233d;padding:20px;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:20px;border:1px solid #33415c;border-left:4px solid #22d3ee;">
    <h3 style="color:#bbdefb;margin-top:0;">🔭 Business Background</h3>
    <p><strong>Careers office:</strong> gives information on pathways, tracks, subjects and careers; organises career talks and days. <strong>Mentorship:</strong> pairs learners with role models — teachers, older learners or professionals — who guide and encourage. <strong>Chaplaincy:</strong> offers spiritual and moral guidance, for example through the chaplain, religious clubs and worship. <strong>Welfare:</strong> looks after learners’ basic needs, such as help with uniforms, meals or fees, and general well-being. <strong>Alumni:</strong> former students who return to share experiences, mentor, give talks or support projects. <strong>Wellness:</strong> guidance and counselling, health services and programmes that support mental, emotional and physical health. <strong>Clubs and societies:</strong> help discover talents, build teamwork and leadership. <strong>Importance:</strong> they support <em>holistic development</em> — academic, social, emotional, spiritual, physical and career growth; they help learners make informed choices, cope with stress and build confidence.</p>
    </div>
